nt_capabilities_service.ts:79:    constructor(provider: AgentCapabilitiesProvider = configuredProfileProvider) {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_types.ts:5:export const PROJECT_CONFIG_PATH = 'md2.config.json'\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:14:Provide a global theme service (light/dark, flat look, configurable color scheme with preview, configurable markdown styles with pre-built defaults) that all components refresh from, including reading the theme in Electron before the main window is created.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:17:Theming is minimal ([[F-004]]): `createAppTheme(mode)` in `theme/appTheme.ts` just returns `createTheme({ palette: { mode } })`, and `useThemeMode` (`theme/useThemeMode.ts`) tracks light/dark, persisting the choice to `localStorage` (`md2.themeMode`) with an OS-preference fallback. `App` builds the theme and provides it via MUI `ThemeProvider`; `mode`/`onToggleTheme` are threaded as props through `MainWindow` and `MainToolbar` rather than read from a service. There is no configurable color scheme, no flat/round/borderless styling, no markdown style config, and `CardTypeConfig` (`data/dataTypes.ts`) has no color. On the desktop, `desktop/main.js` creates the `BrowserWindow` with default chrome and never reads the theme, so the window buttons are unstyled.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:22:- Configurable color scheme: expose editable `primary`/`secondary`/… roles each with `light`/`regular`/`dark` variants, feed them into the palette, and offer a live preview while editing.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:23:- Configurable markdown styles: define a style config mapping each markdown section (title1, title2, caption, body, …) to font/color/size/formatting; ship pre-built defaults (`modern`, `classic`, `serif`, `sans-serif`, `handwritten`) selectable by the user.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:31:- The color scheme (primary/secondary/… with light/regular/dark variants) is user-configurable with a live preview, and the choice persists across restarts.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:32:- Markdown section styling is configurable, with the listed pre-built defaults selectable; the selection persists across restarts.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:3:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:33:        configService.clear()\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:61:    it('loads configured profile overrides and fixed thinking levels without provider credentials', async () => {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:62:        configService.init({\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:63:            desktopConfig: {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agents\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:100:        configService.init()\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_007_markdown_editor.md:17:`@mdxeditor/editor` is installed but still not used by any component in `app/src`; every editing surface is an interim multiline MUI `TextField`. Card view ([[F-005]]) and text view ([[F-006]]) are both implemented and wired through `ProjectWorkspace`, so `ProjectWorkspace` no longer edits a card directly — it delegates to `CardView` and `TextView` and forwards their changes to `DataService`. Card body editing goes through `CardBodyEditor` (used by the desktop `CardBodyDialog` and mobile accordion), whose `onBodyChange` calls `DataService.updateCardBody`; that method already uses the shared `markdownParsingService.replaceBody` to preserve the frontmatter/header block and replace only the body. Text view edits full file content in a per-tab `TextField` and saves via the same `onBodyChange`/`DataService` path. Both `CardBodyEditor` and the text-view editor carry TODO notes that the MDXEditor component and its formatting toolbar land with F-007 and replace them. There is still no shared editor component and no formatting toolbar (sticky or otherwise).\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_007_markdown_editor.md:23:- Replace the current `ProjectWorkspace` textarea path with the shared editor, then reuse the same component in card dialog/mobile accordion and future file tabs.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_017_search.md:21:The top shell is `MainToolbar` (MUI `AppBar`/`Toolbar`) rendered by `MainWindow`; it holds the \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"MD²\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" title, a config `IconButton` and a `toolbarAction` slot (currently `<ThemeControls />` from `app.tsx`). There is no search input in the toolbar. The desktop window is borderless via Electron `titleBarStyle: 'hidden'` with a `titleBarOverlay` in `desktop/main.js`; there is no manual CSS drag region (`-webkit-app-region`) anywhere in the React shell, so a custom drag bar and its non-draggable input/button zones do not yet exist.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_017_search.md:23:Navigation into a card/file is local to `ProjectWorkspace`, which owns `viewMode` (`'cards' | 'text'`). `handleOpenInFileMode(path)` sets a `requestedPath` + `requestedNonce` and switches to text view; `TextView` opens that path as a tab via `useOpenTabs` and can browse background files through its file tree. There is no shared/global \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\"navigate to card or file, keeping current view\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\" API — selecting a background result without changing view mode is not currently supported. Routing exists via `app_navigation` (`navigateTo` / `useAppLocation`, with a `/config` route), but nothing search-related uses it.\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:6:    ProjectConfig,\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:10:import { GithubProjectConfigStorage } from './github_project_config_storage'\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:23:    private readonly configStorage: GithubProjectConfigStorage\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:33:        this.configStorage = new GithubProjectConfigStorage(this.context, gitData, this.writer)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:64:    async loadProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference) {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:65:        return this.configStorage.loadProjectConfig(project)\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:104:    async saveProjectConfig(project: ProjectReference, config: ProjectConfig) {\\\\\\\\napp\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\src\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\services\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\github_storage_service.ts:105:        return this.configStorage.saveProjectConfig(project, config)\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:3:title: config\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:13:> **NOTE 2026-07-11:** The `window.md2GithubAuth` bridge and GitHub OAuth proxy referenced below were removed with OAuth (see [[F_034_github_oauth_cors_proxy]]). GitHub auth is now PAT-only and the `connection` config section no longer exists.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:16:Provide a browsable `/config` page with sections and quick-jump tabs, typed value editors with descriptions, explicit save/cancel, and a global config service that merges values from React-app, desktop-app and project-level sources depending on the connection setup.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:19:Config is still handled by separate feature-specific paths. There is no `/config` route, no router-backed navigation, no config page UI, no draft save/cancel flow and no singleton `ConfigService`. The shared `service_injector` exists and `DataService` registers itself there, but config is passed directly into `DataService.init`.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:21:Project config is a small in-memory object. `createProjectConfig(pushMode)` builds it from hard-coded/default values: working folder `design`, default card types, default card body template and the selected push mode. `ProjectWorkspace` owns the push-mode select, recreates config when opening a GitHub or local project, and reads card types/working folder back from `DataService`. `use_app_bootstrap.ts` restores the last project with auto push mode. No project config file is loaded, merged, validated or saved.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:23:GitHub auth config is read from Vite environment values by `readGithubAuthConfig`; missing `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID` fails fast, optional proxy URL can be absent and scopes default to `repo`. Theme settings are persisted separately in `localStorage` through `useThemeSettings`, not through a general config system.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:25:Electron exposes local data, GitHub OAuth proxy and theme-mode bridges on `window.md2Data`, `window.md2GithubAuth` and `window.md2Theme`. The desktop app URL is resolved from `MD2_APP_URL` with a localhost default. There is no desktop config bridge for editable settings and no project-level config IPC/storage contract.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:27:Tests cover the current focused paths: project/session data behavior, GitHub auth config, theme settings/provider, Electron app URL resolution and desktop theme helpers. There are no config-service merge/validation tests or config-page React tests yet.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:30:- Add a singleton `ConfigService` in `app/src/services/`, registered through `service_injector`, with two-phase initialization and explicit `get`, `set`, `clear`, `loadDraft`, `saveDraft` and `discardDraft` behavior.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:31:- Define config metadata separately from values: key, section, label, description, value type, allowed options/range, default value, source (`react`, `desktop`, `project`) and editability.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:32:- Replace `createProjectConfig(pushMode)` and direct config constants with values from `ConfigService`; affected call sites are `use_app_bootstrap.ts`, `project_workspace.tsx` and `data_service.ts`. They should receive the new config behavior.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:33:- Keep GitHub env config (`github_auth_config.ts`) fail-fast for required build/runtime values, but expose editable connection settings only for values that can be changed safely at runtime.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:34:- In desktop mode, expose desktop config values through the preload bridge. Use main-process IPC only for values that require main-owned Electron APIs.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:35:- Project config is loaded after a project opens, merged over defaults, and saved through the active storage backend. Missing required project config fields fail with clear errors.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:36:- Build `/config` as a real navigable route or URL-backed view. Sections use hash anchors for quick jumps; desktop shows section tabs on the left, mobile shows them below the toolbar.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:37:- The config page edits a draft only. Save validates and applies changes to services; Cancel or leaving the page clears the draft without changing active config.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:40:- `/config` can be opened directly and navigated with browser back/forward, including section hash jumps.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:41:- Config entries are grouped by section and rendered with typed editors: switch for booleans, dropdown for known values, number input or slider for numeric ranges, and short descriptions for all entries.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:42:- Save applies validated changes to the global config service and affected services; Cancel leaves the active config unchanged.\\\\\\\\ndesign\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\F_016_config.md:44:- Opening a project loads project config, merges it over defaults, and uses it for working folder, push mode and card